                            <comment id="30106871" author="spoluri" created="Tue, 16 Jun 2026 01:36:13 +0530"  >&lt;p&gt;Approaches for registration while dealing with dynamic object noise:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pre-filtering (remove before registration):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Ground segmentation (might consider this even in phase 1 depending on results of registration. ground delivers non-discriminative features that can cause poor registration)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Semantic Segmentation - mask out dynamic objects and leave only the background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Robust Registration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Dynamic weighting: iteratively reweighted least squares + point-to-plane ICP?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Normal distribution transforms - instead of points, represent the scene as a grid of probability distributions (aligns really well with probabilistic scene graph architecture for scenescape v2)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;TSDF - accumulate point cloud with voting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Deep learning based:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;FCGF?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;FPFH &amp;amp; TEASER++?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="30012043" author="spoluri" created="Wed, 3 Jun 2026 10:24:31 +0530"  >&lt;p&gt;Assumption (for 2026.2):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;availability of a 3D Scene Mesh so that auto calibration methods are easier to implement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;single camera and single lidar fusion in scenescape&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lidar input will be from Point Pillars model run via DLStreamer&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Goal:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;keep the interface consistent in how cameras and lidars auto calibrate i.e registration with a 3D scene mesh and then localization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;KPI: a 30 second upper bound on localization time for a million point Point Cloud will suffice on PTL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Qualitative expectations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Enables fusion of camera detections and Lidar detections in tracker.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Metrics:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;MSOCE - see that fusion is successful and deduplication happens correctly. In the absence of ground truth, use the camera only run as the ground truth.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Jitter metric - In the absence of ground truth, use the camera only run as the ground truth.&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Implementation considerations:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PCL already contains OneAPI optimizations for different flavors of ICP and can utilize the GPU effectively when configured.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Potential methods considered in prior evaluations: ICP, GICP from PCL. This is not a simple point cloud registration. The point clouds (scene and lidar observation) are not covering the same area. They will have overlap and we need to find a suitable algorithm that can register two point clouds based on the overlap.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The object classes must be aligned for camera and lidar to enable fusion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Acceptable constraint to make the first phase achievable:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The lidar sensor point cloud covers a region completely within the 3D scene point cloud -&amp;gt; GICP should suffice&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Context on future direction of autocalibration service for better design that is aligned long-term:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Eventually the autocalibration service will become the Positioning service i.e go from static positioning with no real-time constraints to dynamic positioning with real-time constraints.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
